window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b373-bbbbfb482fb8e9af.json"]={sha256:"bbbbfb482fb8e9af8e28860933ad3ae7d8a611a0efbcf74bb46d70b168403841",value:{"id":"b373","title":"軌道電路列車占用偵測","titleEn":"Track-circuit train-occupancy detection","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課聚焦軌道電路回路分流與可信占用判讀。從軌道回路電阻帳建立物理或資訊邊界，接著把牽引干擾訊雜比與斷線與供電異常辨識連成可驗證的介面，最後以誤占用維修履歷整理證據。學徒逐一完成機制推導、數值算例、失效辨識及參數實驗，所有練習限定在離線模型或隔離教具，保留假設與量測的不確定度。","summaryEn":"This course studies track-circuit paths shunting and trustworthy occupancy interpretation. Start with resistance accounting for the track circuit to define physical or information boundaries, connect signal quality under traction interference with distinguishing disconnection and supply faults as verifiable interfaces, and organize evidence through maintenance history of false occupancy. Each unit develops a mechanism, numerical example, failure diagnosis and parameter experiment in an offline model or isolated teaching rig, retaining assumptions and measurement uncertainty.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-control","subcategoryTitle":"號誌與營運控制","subcategoryTitleEn":"Signalling and operational control","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-control","learningTags":["rail","rail-control","control"],"architectureFamily":"rail-control","architectureNodes":[["隔離電源","Isolated supply"],["鋼軌回路","Rail circuit"],["輪對分流","Wheelset shunt"],["接收判定","Receiver decision"],["占用證據","Occupancy evidence"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-control","labels":["隔離電源","鋼軌回路","輪對分流","接收判定","占用證據"],"labelsEn":["Isolated supply","Rail circuit","Wheelset shunt","Receiver decision","Occupancy evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創整合工作單，所有輸入均為教學假設而非代表工程實測：先研究軌道回路電阻帳。原創假想教學輸入：激勵電壓 V=12 V；等效電阻 R=8 ohm。公式 y=V/R，代入得 y=1.5 A。邊界：純電阻穩態概念模型，未含交流電抗或任何現場占用判定門檻。敏感度只改 R=8 至 8.8 ohm，輸出變為 1.36364 A；離散計數採整數變化。再獨立研究輪對分流與漏電：原創假想教學輸入：支路一電阻 R1=10 ohm；支路二電阻 R2=40 ohm。公式 y=R1*R2/(R1+R2)，代入得 y=8 ohm。邊界：兩個線性電阻的靜態教具，未模擬頻率選擇接收器。兩個結果不能因同一課程就任意相加，必須先確認單位、因果順序及共同邊界。本單元用隔離低壓回路比較送端、鋼軌和接收端電壓，先畫完整回流路徑再解釋電流變化。最後提出一項量測能區分模型假設失效與儀器偏差，將輸入表、重算結果和適用限制一併交付。","textEn":"Original integrated worksheet; every input is a teaching assumption rather than a measurement from a reference project. First investigate resistance accounting for the track circuit. Original hypothetical teaching inputs: excitation voltage V=12 V; equivalent resistance R=8 ohm. Formula y=V/R gives y=1.5 A. Boundary: Steady resistive teaching model; AC reactance and real occupancy thresholds are not included. For sensitivity, change only R=8 to 8.8 ohm; the output becomes 1.36364 A. Discrete counts use whole-number steps. Independently investigate wheelset shunts and leakage: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: branch one resistance R1=10 ohm; branch two resistance R2=40 ohm. Formula y=R1*R2/(R1+R2) gives y=8 ohm. Boundary: Static teaching circuit with two linear resistors; frequency-selective receivers are not represented. Results cannot be added merely because they belong to the same course: check units, causal sequence and shared boundaries first. Use an isolated low-voltage circuit to compare feed, rail and receiver voltages, drawing the complete return path before interpreting current changes. Propose one measurement distinguishing a failed model assumption from instrument bias, and deliver the input table, recomputed results and applicability limits together.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b373-v16-s1","title":"軌道回路電阻帳與輪對分流與漏電","titleEn":"Resistance accounting for the track circuit & Wheelset shunts and leakage","description":"本階段聚焦「軌道回路電阻帳」與「輪對分流與漏電」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Resistance accounting for the track circuit\" and \"Wheelset shunts and leakage\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b373-v16-01","title":"軌道回路電阻帳：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Resistance accounting for the track circuit: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「軌道回路電阻帳」如何影響軌道電路列車占用偵測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Resistance accounting for the track circuit” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Track-circuit train-occupancy detection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元用隔離低壓回路比較送端、鋼軌和接收端電壓，先畫完整回流路徑再解釋電流變化。電壓與電流的關係取決於完整回路阻抗，不能只看單一導體。簡化電阻模型能用來辨認分流、接觸與漏電的量級，但交流軌道電路還涉及頻率、相位與耦合；量到電壓存在並不等於接收端已可靠判定。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：純電阻穩態概念模型，未含交流電抗或任何現場占用判定門檻。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「軌道回路電阻帳」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Use an isolated low-voltage circuit to compare feed, rail and receiver voltages, drawing the complete return path before interpreting current changes. Voltage-current behaviour depends on the entire circuit rather than one conductor. A resistance model helps reason about shunts, contacts and leakage, while AC track circuits also depend on frequency, phase and coupling. Voltage presence alone does not establish a valid receiver decision. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Steady resistive teaching model; AC reactance and real occupancy thresholds are not included. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Resistance accounting for the track circuit” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：激勵電壓 V=12 V；等效電阻 R=8 ohm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: excitation voltage V=12 V; equivalent resistance R=8 ohm.","failure":"常見誤解：「只量到供電端有電壓就可確認接收端一定正常」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Voltage at the supply terminal proves the receiver is operating correctly.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「軌道回路電阻帳」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Resistance accounting for the track circuit”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-01-k1","title":"軌道回路電阻帳","titleEn":"Resistance accounting for the track circuit","text":"本單元用隔離低壓回路比較送端、鋼軌和接收端電壓，先畫完整回流路徑再解釋電流變化。電壓與電流的關係取決於完整回路阻抗，不能只看單一導體。","textEn":"Use an isolated low-voltage circuit to compare feed, rail and receiver voltages, drawing the complete return path before interpreting current changes. Voltage-current behaviour depends on the entire circuit rather than one conductor.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只量到供電端有電壓就可確認接收端一定正常 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Voltage at the supply terminal proves the receiver is operating correctly. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「軌道回路電阻帳」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Resistance accounting for the track circuit\" is correct?","options":["只量到供電端有電壓就可確認接收端一定正常","本單元用隔離低壓回路比較送端、鋼軌和接收端電壓，先畫完整回流路徑再解釋電流變化。","並聯多一條漏電路徑不會改變整個電路的電流"],"optionsEn":["Voltage at the supply terminal proves the receiver is operating correctly.","Use an isolated low-voltage circuit to compare feed, rail and receiver voltages, drawing the complete return path before interpreting current changes.","Adding a parallel leakage path cannot change the total circuit current."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元用隔離低壓回路比較送端、鋼軌和接收端電壓，先畫完整回流路徑再解釋電流變化。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Use an isolated low-voltage circuit to compare feed, rail and receiver voltages, drawing the complete return path before interpreting current changes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b373-v16-02","title":"軌道回路電阻帳：定量估算","titleEn":"Resistance accounting for the track circuit: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「軌道回路電阻帳」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Resistance accounting for the track circuit” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：激勵電壓 V=12 V；等效電阻 R=8 ohm。公式 y=V/R，代入得 y=1.5 A。邊界：純電阻穩態概念模型，未含交流電抗或任何現場占用判定門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: excitation voltage V=12 V; equivalent resistance R=8 ohm. Formula y=V/R gives y=1.5 A. Boundary: Steady resistive teaching model; AC reactance and real occupancy thresholds are not included. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在完全隔離的低壓教具量測源端與負載端電壓電流，逐一改變接觸或漏電支路。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: On an isolated low-voltage teaching rig, measure source and load voltage/current while changing contact or leakage branches one at a time.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：激勵電壓 V=12 V；等效電阻 R=8 ohm。公式 y=V/R，代入得 y=1.5 A。邊界：純電阻穩態概念模型，未含交流電抗或任何現場占用判定門檻。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: excitation voltage V=12 V; equivalent resistance R=8 ohm. Formula y=V/R gives y=1.5 A. Boundary: Steady resistive teaching model; AC reactance and real occupancy thresholds are not included.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「軌道回路電阻帳」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Resistance accounting for the track circuit\", which statement holds?","options":["總量測電壓越大就能保證訊號品質越好","測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致","原創假想教學輸入：激勵電壓 V=12 V；等效電阻 R=8 ohm。"],"optionsEn":["A larger measured total voltage guarantees better signal quality.","Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: excitation voltage V=12 V; equivalent resistance R=8 ohm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：激勵電壓 V=12 V；等效電阻 R=8 ohm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: excitation voltage V=12 V; equivalent resistance R=8 ohm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b373-v16-03","title":"軌道回路電阻帳：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Resistance accounting for the track circuit: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「軌道回路電阻帳」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Resistance accounting for the track circuit” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在完全隔離的低壓教具量測源端與負載端電壓電流，逐一改變接觸或漏電支路。以「軌道回路電阻帳」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"On an isolated low-voltage teaching rig, measure source and load voltage/current while changing contact or leakage branches one at a time. For resistance accounting for the track circuit, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把等效電阻 R 從 8 改成 8.8 ohm（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 1.5 變為 1.36364 A。先說明「軌道回路電阻帳」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only equivalent resistance R from 8 to 8.8 ohm (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 1.5 to 1.36364 A. Explain the causal direction for resistance accounting for the track circuit, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：接觸阻抗上升與供電下降都會降低電流，可用兩端電壓分布辨認，不能直接在營運軌道上試驗。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Contact resistance and supply drop both reduce current; terminal voltage distribution distinguishes them. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在完全隔離的低壓教具量測源端與負載端電壓電流，逐一改變接觸或漏電支路。以「軌道回路電阻帳」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"On an isolated low-voltage teaching rig, measure source and load voltage/current while changing contact or leakage branches one at a time. For resistance accounting for the track circuit, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把等效電阻 R 從 8 改成 8.8 ohm（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 1.5 變為 1.36364 A。先說明「軌道回路電阻帳」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only equivalent resistance R from 8 to 8.8 ohm (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 1.5 to 1.36364 A. Explain the causal direction for resistance accounting for the track circuit, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「軌道回路電阻帳」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Resistance accounting for the track circuit\"?","options":["在完全隔離的低壓教具量測源端與負載端電壓電流，逐一改變接觸或漏電支路。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障"],"optionsEn":["On an isolated low-voltage teaching rig, measure source and load voltage/current while changing contact or leakage branches one at a time.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在完全隔離的低壓教具量測源端與負載端電壓電流，逐一改變接觸或漏電支路。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"On an isolated low-voltage teaching rig, measure source and load voltage/current while changing contact or leakage branches one at a time. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b373-v16-04","title":"軌道回路電阻帳：失效診斷","titleEn":"Resistance accounting for the track circuit: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「軌道回路電阻帳」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Resistance accounting for the track circuit” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"接觸阻抗上升與供電下降都會降低電流，可用兩端電壓分布辨認，不能直接在營運軌道上試驗。回到「軌道回路電阻帳」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Contact resistance and supply drop both reduce current; terminal voltage distribution distinguishes them. Such experiments do not belong on an operating track. Trace the input chain for resistance accounting for the track circuit. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：純電阻穩態概念模型，未含交流電抗或任何現場占用判定門檻。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Steady resistive teaching model; AC reactance and real occupancy thresholds are not included.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只量到供電端有電壓就可確認接收端一定正常」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Voltage at the supply terminal proves the receiver is operating correctly.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"接觸阻抗上升與供電下降都會降低電流，可用兩端電壓分布辨認，不能直接在營運軌道上試驗。回到「軌道回路電阻帳」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Contact resistance and supply drop both reduce current; terminal voltage distribution distinguishes them. Such experiments do not belong on an operating track. Trace the input chain for resistance accounting for the track circuit. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「軌道回路電阻帳」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Resistance accounting for the track circuit\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","接觸阻抗上升與供電下降都會降低電流，可用兩端電壓分布辨認，不能直接在營運軌道上試驗。","並聯多一條漏電路徑不會改變整個電路的電流"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Contact resistance and supply drop both reduce current; terminal voltage distribution distinguishes them.","Adding a parallel leakage path cannot change the total circuit current."],"answer":1,"explanation":"接觸阻抗上升與供電下降都會降低電流，可用兩端電壓分布辨認，不能直接在營運軌道上試驗。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Contact resistance and supply drop both reduce current; terminal voltage distribution distinguishes them. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b373-v16-05","title":"輪對分流與漏電：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Wheelset shunts and leakage: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「輪對分流與漏電」如何影響軌道電路列車占用偵測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wheelset shunts and leakage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Track-circuit train-occupancy detection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元把輪對支路與道床漏電支路分開，研究不同路徑如何產生相似的接收訊號下降。並聯支路分配電流並降低總等效電阻。新增漏電路徑可能改變接收訊號而不改變供電電壓，乾濕環境的差異因此不能被單純視為量測雜訊；是否代表安全占用仍須由完整的故障安全設計決定。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：兩個線性電阻的靜態教具，未模擬頻率選擇接收器。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「輪對分流與漏電」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate the wheelset path from ballast leakage and examine how different paths can produce similar reductions in the received signal. Parallel paths divide current and reduce equivalent resistance. A leakage path can alter the received signal without changing supply voltage, so differences between dry and wet conditions are not merely measurement noise. Whether a condition produces a safe occupied indication depends on the complete fail-safe design. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Static teaching circuit with two linear resistors; frequency-selective receivers are not represented. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Wheelset shunts and leakage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：支路一電阻 R1=10 ohm；支路二電阻 R2=40 ohm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: branch one resistance R1=10 ohm; branch two resistance R2=40 ohm.","failure":"常見誤解：「並聯多一條漏電路徑不會改變整個電路的電流」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding a parallel leakage path cannot change the total circuit current.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「輪對分流與漏電」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Wheelset shunts and leakage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-05-k1","title":"輪對分流與漏電","titleEn":"Wheelset shunts and leakage","text":"本單元把輪對支路與道床漏電支路分開，研究不同路徑如何產生相似的接收訊號下降。並聯支路分配電流並降低總等效電阻。","textEn":"Separate the wheelset path from ballast leakage and examine how different paths can produce similar reductions in the received signal. Parallel paths divide current and reduce equivalent resistance.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：並聯多一條漏電路徑不會改變整個電路的電流 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding a parallel leakage path cannot change the total circuit current. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「輪對分流與漏電」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wheelset shunts and leakage\" is correct?","options":["並聯多一條漏電路徑不會改變整個電路的電流","濾波越強就能同時得到越快的狀態反應","本單元把輪對支路與道床漏電支路分開，研究不同路徑如何產生相似的接收訊號下降。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a parallel leakage path cannot change the total circuit current.","Stronger filtering always gives a faster state response as well.","Separate the wheelset path from ballast leakage and examine how different paths can produce similar reductions in the received signal."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元把輪對支路與道床漏電支路分開，研究不同路徑如何產生相似的接收訊號下降。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate the wheelset path from ballast leakage and examine how different paths can produce similar reductions in the received signal. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b373-v16-06","title":"輪對分流與漏電：定量估算","titleEn":"Wheelset shunts and leakage: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「輪對分流與漏電」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wheelset shunts and leakage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：支路一電阻 R1=10 ohm；支路二電阻 R2=40 ohm。公式 y=R1*R2/(R1+R2)，代入得 y=8 ohm。邊界：兩個線性電阻的靜態教具，未模擬頻率選擇接收器。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: branch one resistance R1=10 ohm; branch two resistance R2=40 ohm. Formula y=R1*R2/(R1+R2) gives y=8 ohm. Boundary: Static teaching circuit with two linear resistors; frequency-selective receivers are not represented. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：保持激勵相同而分別量支路電流，確認總電流守恆，再比對不同絕緣情境。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Keep excitation fixed, measure branch currents separately, verify current conservation, and compare insulation scenarios.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：支路一電阻 R1=10 ohm；支路二電阻 R2=40 ohm。公式 y=R1*R2/(R1+R2)，代入得 y=8 ohm。邊界：兩個線性電阻的靜態教具，未模擬頻率選擇接收器。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: branch one resistance R1=10 ohm; branch two resistance R2=40 ohm. Formula y=R1*R2/(R1+R2) gives y=8 ohm. Boundary: Static teaching circuit with two linear resistors; frequency-selective receivers are not represented.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「輪對分流與漏電」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wheelset shunts and leakage\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：支路一電阻 R1=10 ohm；支路二電阻 R2=40 ohm。","每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短","任一支路故障即失效時總機率等於兩機率相乘"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: branch one resistance R1=10 ohm; branch two resistance R2=40 ohm.","Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay.","If either branch failure is sufficient, total failure probability equals their product."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：支路一電阻 R1=10 ohm；支路二電阻 R2=40 ohm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: branch one resistance R1=10 ohm; branch two resistance R2=40 ohm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b373-v16-07","title":"輪對分流與漏電：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wheelset shunts and leakage: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「輪對分流與漏電」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Wheelset shunts and leakage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"保持激勵相同而分別量支路電流，確認總電流守恆，再比對不同絕緣情境。以「輪對分流與漏電」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Keep excitation fixed, measure branch currents separately, verify current conservation, and compare insulation scenarios. For wheelset shunts and leakage, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把支路二電阻 R2 從 40 改成 44 ohm（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 8 變為 8.14815 ohm。先說明「輪對分流與漏電」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only branch two resistance R2 from 40 to 44 ohm (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 8 to 8.14815 ohm. Explain the causal direction for wheelset shunts and leakage, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：將漏電誤判為輪對分流會混淆故障來源；量測儀輸入電阻太低也可能自己形成額外分流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing leakage with a wheelset shunt misidentifies the fault; an instrument with low input resistance can itself create a parallel path. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"保持激勵相同而分別量支路電流，確認總電流守恆，再比對不同絕緣情境。以「輪對分流與漏電」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Keep excitation fixed, measure branch currents separately, verify current conservation, and compare insulation scenarios. For wheelset shunts and leakage, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把支路二電阻 R2 從 40 改成 44 ohm（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 8 變為 8.14815 ohm。先說明「輪對分流與漏電」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only branch two resistance R2 from 40 to 44 ohm (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 8 to 8.14815 ohm. Explain the causal direction for wheelset shunts and leakage, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「輪對分流與漏電」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wheelset shunts and leakage\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","保持激勵相同而分別量支路電流，確認總電流守恆，再比對不同絕緣情境。","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Keep excitation fixed, measure branch currents separately, verify current conservation, and compare insulation scenarios.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"保持激勵相同而分別量支路電流，確認總電流守恆，再比對不同絕緣情境。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Keep excitation fixed, measure branch currents separately, verify current conservation, and compare insulation scenarios. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b373-v16-08","title":"輪對分流與漏電：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wheelset shunts and leakage: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「輪對分流與漏電」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Wheelset shunts and leakage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將漏電誤判為輪對分流會混淆故障來源；量測儀輸入電阻太低也可能自己形成額外分流。回到「輪對分流與漏電」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing leakage with a wheelset shunt misidentifies the fault; an instrument with low input resistance can itself create a parallel path. Trace the input chain for wheelset shunts and leakage. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：兩個線性電阻的靜態教具，未模擬頻率選擇接收器。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Static teaching circuit with two linear resistors; frequency-selective receivers are not represented.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「並聯多一條漏電路徑不會改變整個電路的電流」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding a parallel leakage path cannot change the total circuit current.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將漏電誤判為輪對分流會混淆故障來源；量測儀輸入電阻太低也可能自己形成額外分流。回到「輪對分流與漏電」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Confusing leakage with a wheelset shunt misidentifies the fault; an instrument with low input resistance can itself create a parallel path. Trace the input chain for wheelset shunts and leakage. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「輪對分流與漏電」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wheelset shunts and leakage\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","濾波越強就能同時得到越快的狀態反應","將漏電誤判為輪對分流會混淆故障來源；量測儀輸入電阻太低也可能自己形成額外分流。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Stronger filtering always gives a faster state response as well.","Confusing leakage with a wheelset shunt misidentifies the fault; an instrument with low input resistance can itself create a parallel path."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將漏電誤判為輪對分流會混淆故障來源；量測儀輸入電阻太低也可能自己形成額外分流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing leakage with a wheelset shunt misidentifies the fault; an instrument with low input resistance can itself create a parallel path. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b373-v16-s2","title":"輸入濾波與延時與牽引干擾訊雜比","titleEn":"Input filtering and delay & Signal quality under traction interference","description":"本階段聚焦「輸入濾波與延時」與「牽引干擾訊雜比」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Input filtering and delay\" and \"Signal quality under traction interference\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b373-v16-09","title":"輸入濾波與延時：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Input filtering and delay: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「輸入濾波與延時」如何影響軌道電路列車占用偵測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Input filtering and delay” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Track-circuit train-occupancy detection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元以階躍試驗觀察接收端濾波的延遲代價，將短脈衝抑制與真正狀態改變分開。電阻電容時間常數表示一階響應速度，濾除短脈衝也會延後真正的狀態改變。增強濾波與提高反應速度常互相衝突；訊號判定應結合雜訊頻譜與允許延遲，不可只追求顯示平穩。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：線性一階小訊號模型，時間常數不是確定的安全動作延時。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「輸入濾波與延時」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Use a step test to observe the latency cost of receiver filtering, distinguishing suppression of brief pulses from a genuine state change. An RC time constant characterizes first-order response. Suppressing brief pulses also delays genuine state changes, creating a tradeoff between filtering and response. Signal interpretation must consider noise spectra and allowable delay rather than aiming only for a smooth display. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Linear first-order small-signal model; the time constant is not a prescribed safety-action delay. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Input filtering and delay” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：電阻 R=10000 ohm；電容量 C=0.0001 F。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: resistance R=10000 ohm; capacitance C=0.0001 F.","failure":"常見誤解：「濾波越強就能同時得到越快的狀態反應」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Stronger filtering always gives a faster state response as well.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「輸入濾波與延時」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Input filtering and delay”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-09-k1","title":"輸入濾波與延時","titleEn":"Input filtering and delay","text":"本單元以階躍試驗觀察接收端濾波的延遲代價，將短脈衝抑制與真正狀態改變分開。電阻電容時間常數表示一階響應速度，濾除短脈衝也會延後真正的狀態改變。","textEn":"Use a step test to observe the latency cost of receiver filtering, distinguishing suppression of brief pulses from a genuine state change. An RC time constant characterizes first-order response.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：濾波越強就能同時得到越快的狀態反應 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Stronger filtering always gives a faster state response as well. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「輸入濾波與延時」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Input filtering and delay\" is correct?","options":["本單元以階躍試驗觀察接收端濾波的延遲代價，將短脈衝抑制與真正狀態改變分開。","濾波越強就能同時得到越快的狀態反應","總量測電壓越大就能保證訊號品質越好"],"optionsEn":["Use a step test to observe the latency cost of receiver filtering, distinguishing suppression of brief pulses from a genuine state change.","Stronger filtering always gives a faster state response as well.","A larger measured total voltage guarantees better signal quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以階躍試驗觀察接收端濾波的延遲代價，將短脈衝抑制與真正狀態改變分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Use a step test to observe the latency cost of receiver filtering, distinguishing suppression of brief pulses from a genuine state change. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b373-v16-10","title":"輸入濾波與延時：定量估算","titleEn":"Input filtering and delay: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「輸入濾波與延時」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Input filtering and delay” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：電阻 R=10000 ohm；電容量 C=0.0001 F。公式 y=R*C，代入得 y=1 s。邊界：線性一階小訊號模型，時間常數不是確定的安全動作延時。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: resistance R=10000 ohm; capacitance C=0.0001 F. Formula y=R*C gives y=1 s. Boundary: Linear first-order small-signal model; the time constant is not a prescribed safety-action delay. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用已知階躍輸入量測上升與下降曲線，從曲線擬合時間常數並檢查非對稱。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Apply a known step, measure rise and decay, fit the time constant, and inspect response asymmetry.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：電阻 R=10000 ohm；電容量 C=0.0001 F。公式 y=R*C，代入得 y=1 s。邊界：線性一階小訊號模型，時間常數不是確定的安全動作延時。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: resistance R=10000 ohm; capacitance C=0.0001 F. Formula y=R*C gives y=1 s. Boundary: Linear first-order small-signal model; the time constant is not a prescribed safety-action delay.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「輸入濾波與延時」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Input filtering and delay\", which statement holds?","options":["測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致","原創假想教學輸入：電阻 R=10000 ohm；電容量 C=0.0001 F。","裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障"],"optionsEn":["Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: resistance R=10000 ohm; capacitance C=0.0001 F.","Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：電阻 R=10000 ohm；電容量 C=0.0001 F。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: resistance R=10000 ohm; capacitance C=0.0001 F. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b373-v16-11","title":"輸入濾波與延時：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Input filtering and delay: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「輸入濾波與延時」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Input filtering and delay” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用已知階躍輸入量測上升與下降曲線，從曲線擬合時間常數並檢查非對稱。以「輸入濾波與延時」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Apply a known step, measure rise and decay, fit the time constant, and inspect response asymmetry. For input filtering and delay, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把電容量 C 從 0.0001 改成 0.00011 F（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 1 變為 1.1 s。先說明「輸入濾波與延時」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only capacitance C from 0.0001 to 0.00011 F (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 1 to 1.1 s. Explain the causal direction for input filtering and delay, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：濾波過重會延遲異常呈現，電容量漂移則可能讓同一設定在不同溫度下具有不同反應。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Over-filtering delays anomaly indication; capacitance drift can change response with temperature despite unchanged settings. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用已知階躍輸入量測上升與下降曲線，從曲線擬合時間常數並檢查非對稱。以「輸入濾波與延時」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Apply a known step, measure rise and decay, fit the time constant, and inspect response asymmetry. For input filtering and delay, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把電容量 C 從 0.0001 改成 0.00011 F（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 1 變為 1.1 s。先說明「輸入濾波與延時」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only capacitance C from 0.0001 to 0.00011 F (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 1 to 1.1 s. Explain the causal direction for input filtering and delay, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「輸入濾波與延時」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Input filtering and delay\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","系統可用度很高就能直接證明所有故障都是安全的","用已知階躍輸入量測上升與下降曲線，從曲線擬合時間常數並檢查非對稱。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","High system availability directly proves that every failure is safe.","Apply a known step, measure rise and decay, fit the time constant, and inspect response asymmetry."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用已知階躍輸入量測上升與下降曲線，從曲線擬合時間常數並檢查非對稱。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Apply a known step, measure rise and decay, fit the time constant, and inspect response asymmetry. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b373-v16-12","title":"輸入濾波與延時：失效診斷","titleEn":"Input filtering and delay: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「輸入濾波與延時」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Input filtering and delay” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"濾波過重會延遲異常呈現，電容量漂移則可能讓同一設定在不同溫度下具有不同反應。回到「輸入濾波與延時」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Over-filtering delays anomaly indication; capacitance drift can change response with temperature despite unchanged settings. Trace the input chain for input filtering and delay. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：線性一階小訊號模型，時間常數不是確定的安全動作延時。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Linear first-order small-signal model; the time constant is not a prescribed safety-action delay.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「濾波越強就能同時得到越快的狀態反應」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Stronger filtering always gives a faster state response as well.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"濾波過重會延遲異常呈現，電容量漂移則可能讓同一設定在不同溫度下具有不同反應。回到「輸入濾波與延時」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Over-filtering delays anomaly indication; capacitance drift can change response with temperature despite unchanged settings. Trace the input chain for input filtering and delay. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「輸入濾波與延時」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Input filtering and delay\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["濾波過重會延遲異常呈現，電容量漂移則可能讓同一設定在不同溫度下具有不同反應。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","總量測電壓越大就能保證訊號品質越好"],"optionsEn":["Over-filtering delays anomaly indication; capacitance drift can change response with temperature despite unchanged settings.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A larger measured total voltage guarantees better signal quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"濾波過重會延遲異常呈現，電容量漂移則可能讓同一設定在不同溫度下具有不同反應。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Over-filtering delays anomaly indication; capacitance drift can change response with temperature despite unchanged settings. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b373-v16-13","title":"牽引干擾訊雜比：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Signal quality under traction interference: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「牽引干擾訊雜比」如何影響軌道電路列車占用偵測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Signal quality under traction interference” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Track-circuit train-occupancy detection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元比較固定頻寬內的有效訊號和干擾，不以總電壓變大就判斷占用辨識能力改善。以相同阻抗下的電壓比換算訊雜比時使用二十倍對數。訊號與雜訊必須採一致頻寬與有效值定義；只把量測頻寬縮小可能讓數字改善，卻同時刪掉辨識狀態所需的訊息。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：相同阻抗與相同頻寬的均方根電壓，不適用任意峰值比。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「牽引干擾訊雜比」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compare useful signal and interference within a fixed bandwidth rather than assuming that greater total voltage means improved occupancy discrimination. Voltage-ratio signal-to-noise uses twenty times the logarithm when impedances match. Signal and noise must share bandwidth and RMS definitions. Narrowing measurement bandwidth can improve the number while removing information needed to distinguish states. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: RMS voltages with equal impedance and bandwidth; arbitrary peak ratios are not interchangeable. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Signal quality under traction interference” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：訊號有效值 signal=2 V_rms；雜訊有效值 noise=0.1 V_rms。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: signal RMS signal=2 V_rms; noise RMS noise=0.1 V_rms.","failure":"常見誤解：「總量測電壓越大就能保證訊號品質越好」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A larger measured total voltage guarantees better signal quality.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「牽引干擾訊雜比」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Signal quality under traction interference”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-13-k1","title":"牽引干擾訊雜比","titleEn":"Signal quality under traction interference","text":"本單元比較固定頻寬內的有效訊號和干擾，不以總電壓變大就判斷占用辨識能力改善。以相同阻抗下的電壓比換算訊雜比時使用二十倍對數。","textEn":"Compare useful signal and interference within a fixed bandwidth rather than assuming that greater total voltage means improved occupancy discrimination. Voltage-ratio signal-to-noise uses twenty times the logarithm when impedances match.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：總量測電壓越大就能保證訊號品質越好 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A larger measured total voltage guarantees better signal quality. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「牽引干擾訊雜比」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Signal quality under traction interference\" is correct?","options":["總量測電壓越大就能保證訊號品質越好","本單元比較固定頻寬內的有效訊號和干擾，不以總電壓變大就判斷占用辨識能力改善。","每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短"],"optionsEn":["A larger measured total voltage guarantees better signal quality.","Compare useful signal and interference within a fixed bandwidth rather than assuming that greater total voltage means improved occupancy discrimination.","Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元比較固定頻寬內的有效訊號和干擾，不以總電壓變大就判斷占用辨識能力改善。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compare useful signal and interference within a fixed bandwidth rather than assuming that greater total voltage means improved occupancy discrimination. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b373-v16-14","title":"牽引干擾訊雜比：定量估算","titleEn":"Signal quality under traction interference: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「牽引干擾訊雜比」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Signal quality under traction interference” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：訊號有效值 signal=2 V_rms；雜訊有效值 noise=0.1 V_rms。公式 y=20*log10(signal/noise)，代入得 y=26.0206 dB。邊界：相同阻抗與相同頻寬的均方根電壓，不適用任意峰值比。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: signal RMS signal=2 V_rms; noise RMS noise=0.1 V_rms. Formula y=20*log10(signal/noise) gives y=26.0206 dB. Boundary: RMS voltages with equal impedance and bandwidth; arbitrary peak ratios are not interchangeable. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將有訊號與無訊號樣本採同一濾波器處理，保留頻譜與時間波形交叉比對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Process signal-present and signal-absent samples through the same filter, retaining both spectra and time traces.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：訊號有效值 signal=2 V_rms；雜訊有效值 noise=0.1 V_rms。公式 y=20*log10(signal/noise)，代入得 y=26.0206 dB。邊界：相同阻抗與相同頻寬的均方根電壓，不適用任意峰值比。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: signal RMS signal=2 V_rms; noise RMS noise=0.1 V_rms. Formula y=20*log10(signal/noise) gives y=26.0206 dB. Boundary: RMS voltages with equal impedance and bandwidth; arbitrary peak ratios are not interchangeable.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「牽引干擾訊雜比」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Signal quality under traction interference\", which statement holds?","options":["任一支路故障即失效時總機率等於兩機率相乘","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","原創假想教學輸入：訊號有效值 signal=2 V_rms；雜訊有效值 noise=0.1 V_rms。"],"optionsEn":["If either branch failure is sufficient, total failure probability equals their product.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: signal RMS signal=2 V_rms; noise RMS noise=0.1 V_rms."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：訊號有效值 signal=2 V_rms；雜訊有效值 noise=0.1 V_rms。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: signal RMS signal=2 V_rms; noise RMS noise=0.1 V_rms. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b373-v16-15","title":"牽引干擾訊雜比：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Signal quality under traction interference: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「牽引干擾訊雜比」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Signal quality under traction interference” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將有訊號與無訊號樣本採同一濾波器處理，保留頻譜與時間波形交叉比對。以「牽引干擾訊雜比」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Process signal-present and signal-absent samples through the same filter, retaining both spectra and time traces. For signal quality under traction interference, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把雜訊有效值 noise 從 0.1 改成 0.11 V_rms（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 26.0206 變為 25.1927 dB。先說明「牽引干擾訊雜比」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only noise RMS noise from 0.1 to 0.11 V_rms (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 26.0206 to 25.1927 dB. Explain the causal direction for signal quality under traction interference, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：電磁干擾若落在訊號頻帶內，總有效值可能變大但辨識反而變差；飽和也會破壞比例。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: In-band interference may increase total RMS while worsening identification; saturation also destroys the assumed proportionality. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將有訊號與無訊號樣本採同一濾波器處理，保留頻譜與時間波形交叉比對。以「牽引干擾訊雜比」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Process signal-present and signal-absent samples through the same filter, retaining both spectra and time traces. For signal quality under traction interference, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把雜訊有效值 noise 從 0.1 改成 0.11 V_rms（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 26.0206 變為 25.1927 dB。先說明「牽引干擾訊雜比」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only noise RMS noise from 0.1 to 0.11 V_rms (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 26.0206 to 25.1927 dB. Explain the causal direction for signal quality under traction interference, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「牽引干擾訊雜比」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Signal quality under traction interference\"?","options":["將有訊號與無訊號樣本採同一濾波器處理，保留頻譜與時間波形交叉比對。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只量到供電端有電壓就可確認接收端一定正常"],"optionsEn":["Process signal-present and signal-absent samples through the same filter, retaining both spectra and time traces.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Voltage at the supply terminal proves the receiver is operating correctly."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將有訊號與無訊號樣本採同一濾波器處理，保留頻譜與時間波形交叉比對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Process signal-present and signal-absent samples through the same filter, retaining both spectra and time traces. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b373-v16-16","title":"牽引干擾訊雜比：失效診斷","titleEn":"Signal quality under traction interference: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「牽引干擾訊雜比」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Signal quality under traction interference” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"電磁干擾若落在訊號頻帶內，總有效值可能變大但辨識反而變差；飽和也會破壞比例。回到「牽引干擾訊雜比」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"In-band interference may increase total RMS while worsening identification; saturation also destroys the assumed proportionality. Trace the input chain for signal quality under traction interference. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：相同阻抗與相同頻寬的均方根電壓，不適用任意峰值比。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: RMS voltages with equal impedance and bandwidth; arbitrary peak ratios are not interchangeable.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「總量測電壓越大就能保證訊號品質越好」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A larger measured total voltage guarantees better signal quality.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"電磁干擾若落在訊號頻帶內，總有效值可能變大但辨識反而變差；飽和也會破壞比例。回到「牽引干擾訊雜比」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"In-band interference may increase total RMS while worsening identification; saturation also destroys the assumed proportionality. Trace the input chain for signal quality under traction interference. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「牽引干擾訊雜比」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Signal quality under traction interference\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","電磁干擾若落在訊號頻帶內，總有效值可能變大但辨識反而變差；飽和也會破壞比例。","每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","In-band interference may increase total RMS while worsening identification; saturation also destroys the assumed proportionality.","Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay."],"answer":1,"explanation":"電磁干擾若落在訊號頻帶內，總有效值可能變大但辨識反而變差；飽和也會破壞比例。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"In-band interference may increase total RMS while worsening identification; saturation also destroys the assumed proportionality. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b373-v16-s3","title":"偵測至聯鎖交接與占用事件時間校核","titleEn":"Detection-to-interlocking handoff & Checking occupancy-event timing","description":"本階段聚焦「偵測至聯鎖交接」與「占用事件時間校核」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Detection-to-interlocking handoff\" and \"Checking occupancy-event timing\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b373-v16-17","title":"偵測至聯鎖交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Detection-to-interlocking handoff: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「偵測至聯鎖交接」如何影響軌道電路列車占用偵測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Detection-to-interlocking handoff” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Track-circuit train-occupancy detection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元沿回路量測、接收判定和聯鎖採用追蹤時間，檢查介面等待是否被各自量測漏掉。端到端延遲由量測、通訊、運算與致動串接而成。改善最快的一段通常影響有限，且平均延遲不能代表最壞尾端；定義一致的起訖事件，才能避免子系統都量到好看的數值卻漏掉交接等待。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：各階段串行且時間確定，沒有平行重疊或隨機尾端。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「偵測至聯鎖交接」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Trace timing from circuit measurement through receiver decision to interlocking use, checking for interface waits omitted by separate measurements. End-to-end delay spans sensing, communication, computation and actuation. Improving the fastest stage often yields little benefit, and mean latency does not represent its worst tail. Consistent start and end events prevent subsystems from reporting attractive numbers while overlooking handoff queues. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Deterministic serial stages without overlap or random latency tails. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Detection-to-interlocking handoff” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：量測時間 sense=0.03 s；網路時間 network=0.08 s；運算時間 compute=0.02 s；致動時間 actuate=0.12 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensing time sense=0.03 s; network time network=0.08 s; computation time compute=0.02 s; actuation time actuate=0.12 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「偵測至聯鎖交接」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Detection-to-interlocking handoff”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-17-k1","title":"偵測至聯鎖交接","titleEn":"Detection-to-interlocking handoff","text":"本單元沿回路量測、接收判定和聯鎖採用追蹤時間，檢查介面等待是否被各自量測漏掉。端到端延遲由量測、通訊、運算與致動串接而成。","textEn":"Trace timing from circuit measurement through receiver decision to interlocking use, checking for interface waits omitted by separate measurements. End-to-end delay spans sensing, communication, computation and actuation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「偵測至聯鎖交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Detection-to-interlocking handoff\" is correct?","options":["每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短","測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致","本單元沿回路量測、接收判定和聯鎖採用追蹤時間，檢查介面等待是否被各自量測漏掉。"],"optionsEn":["Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay.","Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.","Trace timing from circuit measurement through receiver decision to interlocking use, checking for interface waits omitted by separate measurements."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元沿回路量測、接收判定和聯鎖採用追蹤時間，檢查介面等待是否被各自量測漏掉。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Trace timing from circuit measurement through receiver decision to interlocking use, checking for interface waits omitted by separate measurements. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b373-v16-18","title":"偵測至聯鎖交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Detection-to-interlocking handoff: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「偵測至聯鎖交接」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Detection-to-interlocking handoff” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：量測時間 sense=0.03 s；網路時間 network=0.08 s；運算時間 compute=0.02 s；致動時間 actuate=0.12 s。公式 y=sense+network+compute+actuate，代入得 y=0.25 s。邊界：各階段串行且時間確定，沒有平行重疊或隨機尾端。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensing time sense=0.03 s; network time network=0.08 s; computation time compute=0.02 s; actuation time actuate=0.12 s. Formula y=sense+network+compute+actuate gives y=0.25 s. Boundary: Deterministic serial stages without overlap or random latency tails. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿同一事件編號串接時間戳，檢查每一段邊界是否重疊或漏算，並注入負載重測。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Follow one event identifier through timestamps, check stage boundaries for overlap or gaps, and repeat under injected load.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：量測時間 sense=0.03 s；網路時間 network=0.08 s；運算時間 compute=0.02 s；致動時間 actuate=0.12 s。公式 y=sense+network+compute+actuate，代入得 y=0.25 s。邊界：各階段串行且時間確定，沒有平行重疊或隨機尾端。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensing time sense=0.03 s; network time network=0.08 s; computation time compute=0.02 s; actuation time actuate=0.12 s. Formula y=sense+network+compute+actuate gives y=0.25 s. Boundary: Deterministic serial stages without overlap or random latency tails.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「偵測至聯鎖交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Detection-to-interlocking handoff\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：量測時間 sense=0.03 s。","裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障","系統可用度很高就能直接證明所有故障都是安全的"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensing time sense=0.03 s; network time network=0.08 s; computation time compute=0.02 s; actuation time actuate=0.12 s.","Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures.","High system availability directly proves that every failure is safe."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：量測時間 sense=0.03 s；網路時間 network=0.08 s；運算時間 compute=0.02 s；致動時間 actuate=0.12 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensing time sense=0.03 s; network time network=0.08 s; computation time compute=0.02 s; actuation time actuate=0.12 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b373-v16-19","title":"偵測至聯鎖交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Detection-to-interlocking handoff: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「偵測至聯鎖交接」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Detection-to-interlocking handoff” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿同一事件編號串接時間戳，檢查每一段邊界是否重疊或漏算，並注入負載重測。以「偵測至聯鎖交接」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Follow one event identifier through timestamps, check stage boundaries for overlap or gaps, and repeat under injected load. For detection-to-interlocking handoff, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把網路時間 network 從 0.08 改成 0.088 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.25 變為 0.258 s。先說明「偵測至聯鎖交接」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only network time network from 0.08 to 0.088 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.25 to 0.258 s. Explain the causal direction for detection-to-interlocking handoff, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：時間基準不同可造成負延遲假象；漏記排隊會使快速單元測試無法預測整合表現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Different clock references can create apparently negative delays; omitted queues prevent fast unit tests from predicting integrated performance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿同一事件編號串接時間戳，檢查每一段邊界是否重疊或漏算，並注入負載重測。以「偵測至聯鎖交接」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Follow one event identifier through timestamps, check stage boundaries for overlap or gaps, and repeat under injected load. For detection-to-interlocking handoff, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把網路時間 network 從 0.08 改成 0.088 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.25 變為 0.258 s。先說明「偵測至聯鎖交接」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only network time network from 0.08 to 0.088 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.25 to 0.258 s. Explain the causal direction for detection-to-interlocking handoff, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「偵測至聯鎖交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Detection-to-interlocking handoff\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","沿同一事件編號串接時間戳，檢查每一段邊界是否重疊或漏算，並注入負載重測。","並聯多一條漏電路徑不會改變整個電路的電流"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Follow one event identifier through timestamps, check stage boundaries for overlap or gaps, and repeat under injected load.","Adding a parallel leakage path cannot change the total circuit current."],"answer":1,"explanation":"沿同一事件編號串接時間戳，檢查每一段邊界是否重疊或漏算，並注入負載重測。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Follow one event identifier through timestamps, check stage boundaries for overlap or gaps, and repeat under injected load. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b373-v16-20","title":"偵測至聯鎖交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Detection-to-interlocking handoff: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「偵測至聯鎖交接」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Detection-to-interlocking handoff” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"時間基準不同可造成負延遲假象；漏記排隊會使快速單元測試無法預測整合表現。回到「偵測至聯鎖交接」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Different clock references can create apparently negative delays; omitted queues prevent fast unit tests from predicting integrated performance. Trace the input chain for detection-to-interlocking handoff. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：各階段串行且時間確定，沒有平行重疊或隨機尾端。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Deterministic serial stages without overlap or random latency tails.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"時間基準不同可造成負延遲假象；漏記排隊會使快速單元測試無法預測整合表現。回到「偵測至聯鎖交接」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Different clock references can create apparently negative delays; omitted queues prevent fast unit tests from predicting integrated performance. Trace the input chain for detection-to-interlocking handoff. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「偵測至聯鎖交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Detection-to-interlocking handoff\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致","時間基準不同可造成負延遲假象；漏記排隊會使快速單元測試無法預測整合表現。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.","Different clock references can create apparently negative delays; omitted queues prevent fast unit tests from predicting integrated performance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"時間基準不同可造成負延遲假象；漏記排隊會使快速單元測試無法預測整合表現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Different clock references can create apparently negative delays; omitted queues prevent fast unit tests from predicting integrated performance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b373-v16-21","title":"占用事件時間校核：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Checking occupancy-event timing: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「占用事件時間校核」如何影響軌道電路列車占用偵測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Checking occupancy-event timing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Track-circuit train-occupancy detection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元將實際模型輪對通過與接收輸出放在同一時基，分開時鐘偏差及接收反應時間。時鐘頻率偏差會隨時間累積成時間差，校時瞬間的偏移與之不同。多系統事件排序若依不同時鐘，可能把因果順序顛倒；校時跳變又會使量測區間長度失真，所以需記錄時鐘品質與校正事件。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：固定頻率偏差的線性累積，忽略溫度漂移與校時伺服動態。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「占用事件時間校核」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Place model-wheelset passage and receiver output on one timebase, separating clock offset from receiver response time. Clock frequency error accumulates into time offset and differs from initial synchronization offset. Ordering multisystem events on different clocks can reverse apparent causality. Synchronization jumps can distort interval lengths, so clock quality and correction events must be recorded. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Linear accumulation at fixed frequency offset; temperature drift and synchronization-servo dynamics are omitted. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Checking occupancy-event timing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：時鐘頻率偏差 drift=20 ppm；未校時期間 duration=3600 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: clock frequency offset drift=20 ppm; unsynchronized interval duration=3600 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「占用事件時間校核」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Checking occupancy-event timing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-21-k1","title":"占用事件時間校核","titleEn":"Checking occupancy-event timing","text":"本單元將實際模型輪對通過與接收輸出放在同一時基，分開時鐘偏差及接收反應時間。時鐘頻率偏差會隨時間累積成時間差，校時瞬間的偏移與之不同。","textEn":"Place model-wheelset passage and receiver output on one timebase, separating clock offset from receiver response time. Clock frequency error accumulates into time offset and differs from initial synchronization offset.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「占用事件時間校核」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Checking occupancy-event timing\" is correct?","options":["本單元將實際模型輪對通過與接收輸出放在同一時基，分開時鐘偏差及接收反應時間。","測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致","任一支路故障即失效時總機率等於兩機率相乘"],"optionsEn":["Place model-wheelset passage and receiver output on one timebase, separating clock offset from receiver response time.","Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.","If either branch failure is sufficient, total failure probability equals their product."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元將實際模型輪對通過與接收輸出放在同一時基，分開時鐘偏差及接收反應時間。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Place model-wheelset passage and receiver output on one timebase, separating clock offset from receiver response time. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b373-v16-22","title":"占用事件時間校核：定量估算","titleEn":"Checking occupancy-event timing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「占用事件時間校核」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Checking occupancy-event timing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：時鐘頻率偏差 drift=20 ppm；未校時期間 duration=3600 s。公式 y=drift*1e-6*duration，代入得 y=0.072 s。邊界：固定頻率偏差的線性累積，忽略溫度漂移與校時伺服動態。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: clock frequency offset drift=20 ppm; unsynchronized interval duration=3600 s. Formula y=drift*1e-6*duration gives y=0.072 s. Boundary: Linear accumulation at fixed frequency offset; temperature drift and synchronization-servo dynamics are omitted. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用獨立時間基準比較多個時刻的偏移，從斜率分辨頻率誤差與一次性跳變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare offsets at several times against an independent reference, using slope to distinguish frequency error from a one-time jump.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：時鐘頻率偏差 drift=20 ppm；未校時期間 duration=3600 s。公式 y=drift*1e-6*duration，代入得 y=0.072 s。邊界：固定頻率偏差的線性累積，忽略溫度漂移與校時伺服動態。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: clock frequency offset drift=20 ppm; unsynchronized interval duration=3600 s. Formula y=drift*1e-6*duration gives y=0.072 s. Boundary: Linear accumulation at fixed frequency offset; temperature drift and synchronization-servo dynamics are omitted.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「占用事件時間校核」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Checking occupancy-event timing\", which statement holds?","options":["測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","原創假想教學輸入：時鐘頻率偏差 drift=20 ppm；未校時期間 duration=3600 s。","只量到供電端有電壓就可確認接收端一定正常"],"optionsEn":["One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: clock frequency offset drift=20 ppm; unsynchronized interval duration=3600 s.","Voltage at the supply terminal proves the receiver is operating correctly."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：時鐘頻率偏差 drift=20 ppm；未校時期間 duration=3600 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: clock frequency offset drift=20 ppm; unsynchronized interval duration=3600 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b373-v16-23","title":"占用事件時間校核：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Checking occupancy-event timing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「占用事件時間校核」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Checking occupancy-event timing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用獨立時間基準比較多個時刻的偏移，從斜率分辨頻率誤差與一次性跳變。以「占用事件時間校核」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare offsets at several times against an independent reference, using slope to distinguish frequency error from a one-time jump. For checking occupancy-event timing, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把未校時期間 duration 從 3600 改成 3960 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.072 變為 0.0792 s。先說明「占用事件時間校核」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only unsynchronized interval duration from 3600 to 3960 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.072 to 0.0792 s. Explain the causal direction for checking occupancy-event timing, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：只對齊開始時刻卻忽略頻率漂移，會讓長測試中的事件逐漸錯位，並誤判通訊延遲。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Aligning only the initial instant leaves frequency drift uncorrected, progressively misaligning events and suggesting false network delay. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用獨立時間基準比較多個時刻的偏移，從斜率分辨頻率誤差與一次性跳變。以「占用事件時間校核」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Compare offsets at several times against an independent reference, using slope to distinguish frequency error from a one-time jump. For checking occupancy-event timing, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把未校時期間 duration 從 3600 改成 3960 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.072 變為 0.0792 s。先說明「占用事件時間校核」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only unsynchronized interval duration from 3600 to 3960 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.072 to 0.0792 s. Explain the causal direction for checking occupancy-event timing, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「占用事件時間校核」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Checking occupancy-event timing\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","濾波越強就能同時得到越快的狀態反應","用獨立時間基準比較多個時刻的偏移，從斜率分辨頻率誤差與一次性跳變。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Stronger filtering always gives a faster state response as well.","Compare offsets at several times against an independent reference, using slope to distinguish frequency error from a one-time jump."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用獨立時間基準比較多個時刻的偏移，從斜率分辨頻率誤差與一次性跳變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare offsets at several times against an independent reference, using slope to distinguish frequency error from a one-time jump. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b373-v16-24","title":"占用事件時間校核：失效診斷","titleEn":"Checking occupancy-event timing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「占用事件時間校核」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Checking occupancy-event timing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只對齊開始時刻卻忽略頻率漂移，會讓長測試中的事件逐漸錯位，並誤判通訊延遲。回到「占用事件時間校核」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Aligning only the initial instant leaves frequency drift uncorrected, progressively misaligning events and suggesting false network delay. Trace the input chain for checking occupancy-event timing. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：固定頻率偏差的線性累積，忽略溫度漂移與校時伺服動態。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Linear accumulation at fixed frequency offset; temperature drift and synchronization-servo dynamics are omitted.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只對齊開始時刻卻忽略頻率漂移，會讓長測試中的事件逐漸錯位，並誤判通訊延遲。回到「占用事件時間校核」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Aligning only the initial instant leaves frequency drift uncorrected, progressively misaligning events and suggesting false network delay. Trace the input chain for checking occupancy-event timing. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「占用事件時間校核」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Checking occupancy-event timing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只對齊開始時刻卻忽略頻率漂移，會讓長測試中的事件逐漸錯位，並誤判通訊延遲。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","任一支路故障即失效時總機率等於兩機率相乘"],"optionsEn":["Aligning only the initial instant leaves frequency drift uncorrected, progressively misaligning events and suggesting false network delay.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","If either branch failure is sufficient, total failure probability equals their product."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只對齊開始時刻卻忽略頻率漂移，會讓長測試中的事件逐漸錯位，並誤判通訊延遲。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Aligning only the initial instant leaves frequency drift uncorrected, progressively misaligning events and suggesting false network delay. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b373-v16-s4","title":"斷線與供電異常辨識與接收鏈共同原因","titleEn":"Distinguishing disconnection and supply faults & Common causes in receiving chains","description":"本階段聚焦「斷線與供電異常辨識」與「接收鏈共同原因」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Distinguishing disconnection and supply faults\" and \"Common causes in receiving chains\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b373-v16-25","title":"斷線與供電異常辨識：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Distinguishing disconnection and supply faults: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「斷線與供電異常辨識」如何影響軌道電路列車占用偵測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Distinguishing disconnection and supply faults” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Track-circuit train-occupancy detection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元把可能造成訊號消失的回路斷線與供電異常列成失效樹，要求可區分原因的觀測。只要任一支路失效就產生頂事件時，需計算聯集而不是把兩機率相乘。獨立假設允許扣掉交集的乘積，若共享電源、環境或軟體則交集另有結構；事件樹和失效樹必須保持同一任務時間。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：兩事件獨立且機率屬同一任務期間，並非每小時危險失效率。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「斷線與供電異常辨識」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Build a fault tree for circuit disconnection and supply problems that can both remove a signal, requiring observations that distinguish the causes. When either branch can trigger the top event, the relevant probability is a union rather than a product. Independence permits the intersection to be written as a product; shared power, environment or software changes that intersection. Event and fault trees must use the same mission duration. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Two independent events over one mission interval, not a dangerous-failure rate per hour. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Distinguishing disconnection and supply faults” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：事件一機率 p1=0.001 1；事件二機率 p2=0.002 1。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: event one probability p1=0.001 1; event two probability p2=0.002 1.","failure":"常見誤解：「任一支路故障即失效時總機率等於兩機率相乘」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If either branch failure is sufficient, total failure probability equals their product.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「斷線與供電異常辨識」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Distinguishing disconnection and supply faults”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-25-k1","title":"斷線與供電異常辨識","titleEn":"Distinguishing disconnection and supply faults","text":"本單元把可能造成訊號消失的回路斷線與供電異常列成失效樹，要求可區分原因的觀測。只要任一支路失效就產生頂事件時，需計算聯集而不是把兩機率相乘。","textEn":"Build a fault tree for circuit disconnection and supply problems that can both remove a signal, requiring observations that distinguish the causes. When either branch can trigger the top event, the relevant probability is a union rather than a product.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：任一支路故障即失效時總機率等於兩機率相乘 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If either branch failure is sufficient, total failure probability equals their product. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「斷線與供電異常辨識」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Distinguishing disconnection and supply faults\" is correct?","options":["任一支路故障即失效時總機率等於兩機率相乘","本單元把可能造成訊號消失的回路斷線與供電異常列成失效樹，要求可區分原因的觀測。","裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障"],"optionsEn":["If either branch failure is sufficient, total failure probability equals their product.","Build a fault tree for circuit disconnection and supply problems that can both remove a signal, requiring observations that distinguish the causes.","Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元把可能造成訊號消失的回路斷線與供電異常列成失效樹，要求可區分原因的觀測。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Build a fault tree for circuit disconnection and supply problems that can both remove a signal, requiring observations that distinguish the causes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b373-v16-26","title":"斷線與供電異常辨識：定量估算","titleEn":"Distinguishing disconnection and supply faults: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「斷線與供電異常辨識」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Distinguishing disconnection and supply faults” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：事件一機率 p1=0.001 1；事件二機率 p2=0.002 1。公式 y=p1+p2-p1*p2，代入得 y=0.002998 1。邊界：兩事件獨立且機率屬同一任務期間，並非每小時危險失效率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: event one probability p1=0.001 1; event two probability p2=0.002 1. Formula y=p1+p2-p1*p2 gives y=0.002998 1. Boundary: Two independent events over one mission interval, not a dangerous-failure rate per hour. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先畫頂事件邏輯再代機率，明列共享資源並檢查事件時間窗是否一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw top-event logic before inserting probabilities, list shared resources, and check consistent time windows.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：事件一機率 p1=0.001 1；事件二機率 p2=0.002 1。公式 y=p1+p2-p1*p2，代入得 y=0.002998 1。邊界：兩事件獨立且機率屬同一任務期間，並非每小時危險失效率。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: event one probability p1=0.001 1; event two probability p2=0.002 1. Formula y=p1+p2-p1*p2 gives y=0.002998 1. Boundary: Two independent events over one mission interval, not a dangerous-failure rate per hour.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「斷線與供電異常辨識」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Distinguishing disconnection and supply faults\", which statement holds?","options":["系統可用度很高就能直接證明所有故障都是安全的","並聯多一條漏電路徑不會改變整個電路的電流","原創假想教學輸入：事件一機率 p1=0.001 1；事件二機率 p2=0.002 1。"],"optionsEn":["High system availability directly proves that every failure is safe.","Adding a parallel leakage path cannot change the total circuit current.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: event one probability p1=0.001 1; event two probability p2=0.002 1."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：事件一機率 p1=0.001 1；事件二機率 p2=0.002 1。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: event one probability p1=0.001 1; event two probability p2=0.002 1. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b373-v16-27","title":"斷線與供電異常辨識：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Distinguishing disconnection and supply faults: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「斷線與供電異常辨識」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Distinguishing disconnection and supply faults” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先畫頂事件邏輯再代機率，明列共享資源並檢查事件時間窗是否一致。以「斷線與供電異常辨識」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw top-event logic before inserting probabilities, list shared resources, and check consistent time windows. For distinguishing disconnection and supply faults, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把事件一機率 p1 從 0.001 改成 0.0011 1（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.002998 變為 0.0030978 1。先說明「斷線與供電異常辨識」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only event one probability p1 from 0.001 to 0.0011 1 (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.002998 to 0.0030978 1. Explain the causal direction for distinguishing disconnection and supply faults, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：把聯集誤寫成交集會低估危險；混合年度機率與每小時機率則使結果失去量綱意義。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing a union with an intersection understates risk; mixing annual and hourly probabilities destroys the intended meaning. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先畫頂事件邏輯再代機率，明列共享資源並檢查事件時間窗是否一致。以「斷線與供電異常辨識」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Draw top-event logic before inserting probabilities, list shared resources, and check consistent time windows. For distinguishing disconnection and supply faults, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把事件一機率 p1 從 0.001 改成 0.0011 1（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.002998 變為 0.0030978 1。先說明「斷線與供電異常辨識」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only event one probability p1 from 0.001 to 0.0011 1 (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.002998 to 0.0030978 1. Explain the causal direction for distinguishing disconnection and supply faults, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「斷線與供電異常辨識」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Distinguishing disconnection and supply faults\"?","options":["先畫頂事件邏輯再代機率，明列共享資源並檢查事件時間窗是否一致。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","總量測電壓越大就能保證訊號品質越好"],"optionsEn":["Draw top-event logic before inserting probabilities, list shared resources, and check consistent time windows.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A larger measured total voltage guarantees better signal quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"先畫頂事件邏輯再代機率，明列共享資源並檢查事件時間窗是否一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw top-event logic before inserting probabilities, list shared resources, and check consistent time windows. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b373-v16-28","title":"斷線與供電異常辨識：失效診斷","titleEn":"Distinguishing disconnection and supply faults: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「斷線與供電異常辨識」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Distinguishing disconnection and supply faults” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把聯集誤寫成交集會低估危險；混合年度機率與每小時機率則使結果失去量綱意義。回到「斷線與供電異常辨識」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing a union with an intersection understates risk; mixing annual and hourly probabilities destroys the intended meaning. Trace the input chain for distinguishing disconnection and supply faults. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：兩事件獨立且機率屬同一任務期間，並非每小時危險失效率。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Two independent events over one mission interval, not a dangerous-failure rate per hour.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「任一支路故障即失效時總機率等於兩機率相乘」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If either branch failure is sufficient, total failure probability equals their product.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把聯集誤寫成交集會低估危險；混合年度機率與每小時機率則使結果失去量綱意義。回到「斷線與供電異常辨識」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Confusing a union with an intersection understates risk; mixing annual and hourly probabilities destroys the intended meaning. Trace the input chain for distinguishing disconnection and supply faults. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「斷線與供電異常辨識」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Distinguishing disconnection and supply faults\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把聯集誤寫成交集會低估危險；混合年度機率與每小時機率則使結果失去量綱意義。","裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Confusing a union with an intersection understates risk; mixing annual and hourly probabilities destroys the intended meaning.","Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把聯集誤寫成交集會低估危險；混合年度機率與每小時機率則使結果失去量綱意義。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing a union with an intersection understates risk; mixing annual and hourly probabilities destroys the intended meaning. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b373-v16-29","title":"接收鏈共同原因：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Common causes in receiving chains: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「接收鏈共同原因」如何影響軌道電路列車占用偵測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Common causes in receiving chains” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Track-circuit train-occupancy detection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元檢查重複接收器是否共用軌道輸入與電源，說明雙設備無法自行消除輸入共同失效。兩支路都失效才失去功能的架構可降低獨立故障貢獻，卻不能消除共同原因。共同電源、相同軟體缺陷或同處淹水會同時影響兩支路；因此增加硬體數量不能取代分離、異質性與失效偵測的證據。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：共同原因先發生的簡化條件模型，其餘支路相互獨立；非安全等級認證。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「接收鏈共同原因」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Check whether duplicated receivers share the track input and power supply, explaining why duplication cannot remove a common input failure by itself. A function lost only when both branches fail can reduce independent contributions but cannot eliminate common causes. Shared power, identical software defects or flooding at one location can affect both branches. More hardware does not replace evidence for separation, diversity and fault detection. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Simple conditional model with common cause considered first and remaining branches independent; no safety-level certification is implied. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Common causes in receiving chains” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：獨立支路失效機率 p=0.002 1；共同原因事件機率 common=0.0001 1。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent branch failure probability p=0.002 1; common-cause event probability common=0.0001 1.","failure":"常見誤解：「裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「接收鏈共同原因」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Common causes in receiving chains”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-29-k1","title":"接收鏈共同原因","titleEn":"Common causes in receiving chains","text":"本單元檢查重複接收器是否共用軌道輸入與電源，說明雙設備無法自行消除輸入共同失效。兩支路都失效才失去功能的架構可降低獨立故障貢獻，卻不能消除共同原因。","textEn":"Check whether duplicated receivers share the track input and power supply, explaining why duplication cannot remove a common input failure by itself. A function lost only when both branches fail can reduce independent contributions but cannot eliminate common causes.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接收鏈共同原因」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Common causes in receiving chains\" is correct?","options":["裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","本單元檢查重複接收器是否共用軌道輸入與電源，說明雙設備無法自行消除輸入共同失效。"],"optionsEn":["Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Check whether duplicated receivers share the track input and power supply, explaining why duplication cannot remove a common input failure by itself."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元檢查重複接收器是否共用軌道輸入與電源，說明雙設備無法自行消除輸入共同失效。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Check whether duplicated receivers share the track input and power supply, explaining why duplication cannot remove a common input failure by itself. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b373-v16-30","title":"接收鏈共同原因：定量估算","titleEn":"Common causes in receiving chains: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「接收鏈共同原因」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Common causes in receiving chains” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：獨立支路失效機率 p=0.002 1；共同原因事件機率 common=0.0001 1。公式 y=common+(1-common)*p*p，代入得 y=0.000104 1。邊界：共同原因先發生的簡化條件模型，其餘支路相互獨立；非安全等級認證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent branch failure probability p=0.002 1; common-cause event probability common=0.0001 1. Formula y=common+(1-common)*p*p gives y=0.000104 1. Boundary: Simple conditional model with common cause considered first and remaining branches independent; no safety-level certification is implied. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把獨立與共同原因兩類試驗分開，在隔離試驗台檢查共享介面失效的影響。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Separate independent and common-cause tests, using an isolated bench to examine failures of shared interfaces.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：獨立支路失效機率 p=0.002 1；共同原因事件機率 common=0.0001 1。公式 y=common+(1-common)*p*p，代入得 y=0.000104 1。邊界：共同原因先發生的簡化條件模型，其餘支路相互獨立；非安全等級認證。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent branch failure probability p=0.002 1; common-cause event probability common=0.0001 1. Formula y=common+(1-common)*p*p gives y=0.000104 1. Boundary: Simple conditional model with common cause considered first and remaining branches independent; no safety-level certification is implied.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接收鏈共同原因」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Common causes in receiving chains\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：獨立支路失效機率 p=0.002 1；共同原因事件機率 common=0.0001 1。","只量到供電端有電壓就可確認接收端一定正常","濾波越強就能同時得到越快的狀態反應"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent branch failure probability p=0.002 1; common-cause event probability common=0.0001 1.","Voltage at the supply terminal proves the receiver is operating correctly.","Stronger filtering always gives a faster state response as well."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：獨立支路失效機率 p=0.002 1；共同原因事件機率 common=0.0001 1。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent branch failure probability p=0.002 1; common-cause event probability common=0.0001 1. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b373-v16-31","title":"接收鏈共同原因：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Common causes in receiving chains: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「接收鏈共同原因」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Common causes in receiving chains” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把獨立與共同原因兩類試驗分開，在隔離試驗台檢查共享介面失效的影響。以「接收鏈共同原因」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Separate independent and common-cause tests, using an isolated bench to examine failures of shared interfaces. For common causes in receiving chains, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把共同原因事件機率 common 從 0.0001 改成 0.00011 1（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.000104 變為 0.000114 1。先說明「接收鏈共同原因」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only common-cause event probability common from 0.0001 to 0.00011 1 (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.000104 to 0.000114 1. Explain the causal direction for common causes in receiving chains, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：共享電源中斷會讓看似雙備援同時失去功能，若故障偵測也共用同一支路更可能誤報正常。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Loss of a shared supply can defeat apparently duplicated equipment, especially if fault detection depends on that same branch. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把獨立與共同原因兩類試驗分開，在隔離試驗台檢查共享介面失效的影響。以「接收鏈共同原因」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Separate independent and common-cause tests, using an isolated bench to examine failures of shared interfaces. For common causes in receiving chains, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把共同原因事件機率 common 從 0.0001 改成 0.00011 1（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.000104 變為 0.000114 1。先說明「接收鏈共同原因」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only common-cause event probability common from 0.0001 to 0.00011 1 (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.000104 to 0.000114 1. Explain the causal direction for common causes in receiving chains, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接收鏈共同原因」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Common causes in receiving chains\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","把獨立與共同原因兩類試驗分開，在隔離試驗台檢查共享介面失效的影響。","每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Separate independent and common-cause tests, using an isolated bench to examine failures of shared interfaces.","Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把獨立與共同原因兩類試驗分開，在隔離試驗台檢查共享介面失效的影響。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Separate independent and common-cause tests, using an isolated bench to examine failures of shared interfaces. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b373-v16-32","title":"接收鏈共同原因：失效診斷","titleEn":"Common causes in receiving chains: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「接收鏈共同原因」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Common causes in receiving chains” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"共享電源中斷會讓看似雙備援同時失去功能，若故障偵測也共用同一支路更可能誤報正常。回到「接收鏈共同原因」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Loss of a shared supply can defeat apparently duplicated equipment, especially if fault detection depends on that same branch. Trace the input chain for common causes in receiving chains. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：共同原因先發生的簡化條件模型，其餘支路相互獨立；非安全等級認證。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Simple conditional model with common cause considered first and remaining branches independent; no safety-level certification is implied.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"共享電源中斷會讓看似雙備援同時失去功能，若故障偵測也共用同一支路更可能誤報正常。回到「接收鏈共同原因」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Loss of a shared supply can defeat apparently duplicated equipment, especially if fault detection depends on that same branch. Trace the input chain for common causes in receiving chains. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接收鏈共同原因」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Common causes in receiving chains\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","共享電源中斷會讓看似雙備援同時失去功能，若故障偵測也共用同一支路更可能誤報正常。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Loss of a shared supply can defeat apparently duplicated equipment, especially if fault detection depends on that same branch."],"answer":2,"explanation":"共享電源中斷會讓看似雙備援同時失去功能，若故障偵測也共用同一支路更可能誤報正常。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Loss of a shared supply can defeat apparently duplicated equipment, especially if fault detection depends on that same branch. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b373-v16-s5","title":"乾濕與故障情境矩陣與誤占用維修履歷","titleEn":"Dry wet and fault test matrix & Maintenance history of false occupancy","description":"本階段聚焦「乾濕與故障情境矩陣」與「誤占用維修履歷」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Dry wet and fault test matrix\" and \"Maintenance history of false occupancy\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b373-v16-33","title":"乾濕與故障情境矩陣：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Dry wet and fault test matrix: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「乾濕與故障情境矩陣」如何影響軌道電路列車占用偵測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Dry wet and fault test matrix” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Track-circuit train-occupancy detection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元以教具建立乾濕漏電、接觸變化與干擾案例，明列哪些狀態仍未取得測試證據。測試覆蓋率只對已定義的分母有意義。需求、狀態、轉移與危害各有不同分母，執行很多正常案例仍可能漏掉罕見但重要的交接；同一案例重跑多次不會自動增加獨立需求的覆蓋。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「乾濕與故障情境矩陣」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Build teaching-rig cases for dry/wet leakage, contact changes and interference, explicitly listing states for which test evidence is still absent. Coverage is meaningful only relative to its defined denominator. Requirements, states, transitions and hazards have different denominators. Many normal cases can still omit a rare but important handoff, and repeating one case does not automatically cover additional independent requirements. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Dry wet and fault test matrix” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases.","failure":"常見誤解：「測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「乾濕與故障情境矩陣」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Dry wet and fault test matrix”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-33-k1","title":"乾濕與故障情境矩陣","titleEn":"Dry wet and fault test matrix","text":"本單元以教具建立乾濕漏電、接觸變化與干擾案例，明列哪些狀態仍未取得測試證據。測試覆蓋率只對已定義的分母有意義。","textEn":"Build teaching-rig cases for dry/wet leakage, contact changes and interference, explicitly listing states for which test evidence is still absent. Coverage is meaningful only relative to its defined denominator.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「乾濕與故障情境矩陣」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Dry wet and fault test matrix\" is correct?","options":["本單元以教具建立乾濕漏電、接觸變化與干擾案例，明列哪些狀態仍未取得測試證據。","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","系統可用度很高就能直接證明所有故障都是安全的"],"optionsEn":["Build teaching-rig cases for dry/wet leakage, contact changes and interference, explicitly listing states for which test evidence is still absent.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","High system availability directly proves that every failure is safe."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以教具建立乾濕漏電、接觸變化與干擾案例，明列哪些狀態仍未取得測試證據。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Build teaching-rig cases for dry/wet leakage, contact changes and interference, explicitly listing states for which test evidence is still absent. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b373-v16-34","title":"乾濕與故障情境矩陣：定量估算","titleEn":"Dry wet and fault test matrix: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「乾濕與故障情境矩陣」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Dry wet and fault test matrix” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。公式 y=tested/total，代入得 y=0.8 1。邊界：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Formula y=tested/total gives y=0.8 1. Boundary: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。公式 y=tested/total，代入得 y=0.8 1。邊界：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Formula y=tested/total gives y=0.8 1. Boundary: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「乾濕與故障情境矩陣」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Dry wet and fault test matrix\", which statement holds?","options":["並聯多一條漏電路徑不會改變整個電路的電流","原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。","總量測電壓越大就能保證訊號品質越好"],"optionsEn":["Adding a parallel leakage path cannot change the total circuit current.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases.","A larger measured total voltage guarantees better signal quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b373-v16-35","title":"乾濕與故障情境矩陣：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Dry wet and fault test matrix: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「乾濕與故障情境矩陣」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Dry wet and fault test matrix” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。以「乾濕與故障情境矩陣」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. For dry wet and fault test matrix, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把已執行案例 tested 從 72 改成 73 cases（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.8 變為 0.811111 1。先說明「乾濕與故障情境矩陣」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only executed cases tested from 72 to 73 cases (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.8 to 0.811111 1. Explain the causal direction for dry wet and fault test matrix, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。以「乾濕與故障情境矩陣」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. For dry wet and fault test matrix, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把已執行案例 tested 從 72 改成 73 cases（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.8 變為 0.811111 1。先說明「乾濕與故障情境矩陣」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only executed cases tested from 72 to 73 cases (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.8 to 0.811111 1. Explain the causal direction for dry wet and fault test matrix, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「乾濕與故障情境矩陣」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Dry wet and fault test matrix\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致","建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.","Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b373-v16-36","title":"乾濕與故障情境矩陣：失效診斷","titleEn":"Dry wet and fault test matrix: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「乾濕與故障情境矩陣」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Dry wet and fault test matrix” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。回到「乾濕與故障情境矩陣」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Trace the input chain for dry wet and fault test matrix. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。回到「乾濕與故障情境矩陣」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Trace the input chain for dry wet and fault test matrix. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「乾濕與故障情境矩陣」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Dry wet and fault test matrix\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","系統可用度很高就能直接證明所有故障都是安全的"],"optionsEn":["Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","High system availability directly proves that every failure is safe."],"answer":0,"explanation":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b373-v16-37","title":"誤占用維修履歷：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Maintenance history of false occupancy: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「誤占用維修履歷」如何影響軌道電路列車占用偵測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Maintenance history of false occupancy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Track-circuit train-occupancy detection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元分開保守占用顯示與真正設備失效紀錄，將重複報修合併到同一根因而保留服務影響。可用度描述長時間內能提供服務的比例，故障頻率與修復速度都會影響它。相同可用度可能來自頻繁短停或罕見長停，對旅客與維修資源的影響不同；更不能把高可用度直接解讀為故障發生時一定安全。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：可修復二狀態穩態模型，未含共同原因故障、預防保養與供應鏈等待。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「誤占用維修履歷」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate conservative occupied indications from equipment-failure records, linking repeated reports to one cause while retaining their service impact. Availability describes the fraction of long-run time during which service is possible; both failure frequency and repair duration matter. The same value can arise from frequent brief outages or rare long ones with different passenger and maintenance consequences. High availability does not itself establish safe behaviour during failure. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Repairable two-state steady model; common-cause failures, planned maintenance and supply-chain waiting are excluded. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Maintenance history of false occupancy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：平均故障間隔 mtbf=2000 h；平均修復時間 mttr=4 h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: mean time between failures mtbf=2000 h; mean repair time mttr=4 h.","failure":"常見誤解：「系統可用度很高就能直接證明所有故障都是安全的」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"High system availability directly proves that every failure is safe.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「誤占用維修履歷」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Maintenance history of false occupancy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-37-k1","title":"誤占用維修履歷","titleEn":"Maintenance history of false occupancy","text":"本單元分開保守占用顯示與真正設備失效紀錄，將重複報修合併到同一根因而保留服務影響。可用度描述長時間內能提供服務的比例，故障頻率與修復速度都會影響它。","textEn":"Separate conservative occupied indications from equipment-failure records, linking repeated reports to one cause while retaining their service impact. Availability describes the fraction of long-run time during which service is possible; both failure frequency and repair duration matter.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：系統可用度很高就能直接證明所有故障都是安全的 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: High system availability directly proves that every failure is safe. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「誤占用維修履歷」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Maintenance history of false occupancy\" is correct?","options":["系統可用度很高就能直接證明所有故障都是安全的","本單元分開保守占用顯示與真正設備失效紀錄，將重複報修合併到同一根因而保留服務影響。","只量到供電端有電壓就可確認接收端一定正常"],"optionsEn":["High system availability directly proves that every failure is safe.","Separate conservative occupied indications from equipment-failure records, linking repeated reports to one cause while retaining their service impact.","Voltage at the supply terminal proves the receiver is operating correctly."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元分開保守占用顯示與真正設備失效紀錄，將重複報修合併到同一根因而保留服務影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate conservative occupied indications from equipment-failure records, linking repeated reports to one cause while retaining their service impact. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b373-v16-38","title":"誤占用維修履歷：定量估算","titleEn":"Maintenance history of false occupancy: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「誤占用維修履歷」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Maintenance history of false occupancy” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：平均故障間隔 mtbf=2000 h；平均修復時間 mttr=4 h。公式 y=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)，代入得 y=0.998004 1。邊界：可修復二狀態穩態模型，未含共同原因故障、預防保養與供應鏈等待。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: mean time between failures mtbf=2000 h; mean repair time mttr=4 h. Formula y=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr) gives y=0.998004 1. Boundary: Repairable two-state steady model; common-cause failures, planned maintenance and supply-chain waiting are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分別核對故障起點、服務恢復及完全修復時間，避免把部分恢復誤列為全功能。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Audit failure onset, service restoration and full repair separately rather than counting degraded service as full functionality.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：平均故障間隔 mtbf=2000 h；平均修復時間 mttr=4 h。公式 y=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)，代入得 y=0.998004 1。邊界：可修復二狀態穩態模型，未含共同原因故障、預防保養與供應鏈等待。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: mean time between failures mtbf=2000 h; mean repair time mttr=4 h. Formula y=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr) gives y=0.998004 1. Boundary: Repairable two-state steady model; common-cause failures, planned maintenance and supply-chain waiting are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「誤占用維修履歷」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Maintenance history of false occupancy\", which statement holds?","options":["濾波越強就能同時得到越快的狀態反應","每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短","原創假想教學輸入：平均故障間隔 mtbf=2000 h；平均修復時間 mttr=4 h。"],"optionsEn":["Stronger filtering always gives a faster state response as well.","Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: mean time between failures mtbf=2000 h; mean repair time mttr=4 h."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：平均故障間隔 mtbf=2000 h；平均修復時間 mttr=4 h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: mean time between failures mtbf=2000 h; mean repair time mttr=4 h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b373-v16-39","title":"誤占用維修履歷：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Maintenance history of false occupancy: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「誤占用維修履歷」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Maintenance history of false occupancy” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分別核對故障起點、服務恢復及完全修復時間，避免把部分恢復誤列為全功能。以「誤占用維修履歷」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Audit failure onset, service restoration and full repair separately rather than counting degraded service as full functionality. For maintenance history of false occupancy, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把平均修復時間 mttr 從 4 改成 4.4 h（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.998004 變為 0.997805 1。先說明「誤占用維修履歷」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only mean repair time mttr from 4 to 4.4 h (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.998004 to 0.997805 1. Explain the causal direction for maintenance history of false occupancy, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：刪除長停機紀錄會扭曲平均修復時間；重複報修同一缺陷則會錯估故障頻率。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Removing long outages distorts mean repair time, while duplicate reports of one defect distort failure frequency. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分別核對故障起點、服務恢復及完全修復時間，避免把部分恢復誤列為全功能。以「誤占用維修履歷」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Audit failure onset, service restoration and full repair separately rather than counting degraded service as full functionality. For maintenance history of false occupancy, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把平均修復時間 mttr 從 4 改成 4.4 h（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.998004 變為 0.997805 1。先說明「誤占用維修履歷」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only mean repair time mttr from 4 to 4.4 h (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.998004 to 0.997805 1. Explain the causal direction for maintenance history of false occupancy, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「誤占用維修履歷」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Maintenance history of false occupancy\"?","options":["分別核對故障起點、服務恢復及完全修復時間，避免把部分恢復誤列為全功能。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","任一支路故障即失效時總機率等於兩機率相乘"],"optionsEn":["Audit failure onset, service restoration and full repair separately rather than counting degraded service as full functionality.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","If either branch failure is sufficient, total failure probability equals their product."],"answer":0,"explanation":"分別核對故障起點、服務恢復及完全修復時間，避免把部分恢復誤列為全功能。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Audit failure onset, service restoration and full repair separately rather than counting degraded service as full functionality. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b373-v16-40","title":"誤占用維修履歷：失效診斷","titleEn":"Maintenance history of false occupancy: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b373-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「誤占用維修履歷」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Maintenance history of false occupancy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"刪除長停機紀錄會扭曲平均修復時間；重複報修同一缺陷則會錯估故障頻率。回到「誤占用維修履歷」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Removing long outages distorts mean repair time, while duplicate reports of one defect distort failure frequency. Trace the input chain for maintenance history of false occupancy. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：可修復二狀態穩態模型，未含共同原因故障、預防保養與供應鏈等待。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Repairable two-state steady model; common-cause failures, planned maintenance and supply-chain waiting are excluded.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「系統可用度很高就能直接證明所有故障都是安全的」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"High system availability directly proves that every failure is safe.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b373-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"刪除長停機紀錄會扭曲平均修復時間；重複報修同一缺陷則會錯估故障頻率。回到「誤占用維修履歷」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Removing long outages distorts mean repair time, while duplicate reports of one defect distort failure frequency. Trace the input chain for maintenance history of false occupancy. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b373-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「誤占用維修履歷」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Maintenance history of false occupancy\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","刪除長停機紀錄會扭曲平均修復時間；重複報修同一缺陷則會錯估故障頻率。","只量到供電端有電壓就可確認接收端一定正常"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Removing long outages distorts mean repair time, while duplicate reports of one defect distort failure frequency.","Voltage at the supply terminal proves the receiver is operating correctly."],"answer":1,"explanation":"刪除長停機紀錄會扭曲平均修復時間；重複報修同一缺陷則會錯估故障頻率。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Removing long outages distorts mean repair time, while duplicate reports of one defect distort failure frequency. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b373-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b373-en.svg"}};
